 ## Background
-Pseudo-Volume Noise Compositing is implemented in the "texturinator" project by MangoButtermilch, an unofficial tool for generating procedural textures [S1, unofficial]. It leverages GLSL noise functions (`cnoise`, `snoise`, `voronoi`, `nebulaNoise`) to create layered noise patterns. The technique is designed to work within fragment shaders, mapping 2D UVs to a pseudo-3D space to simulate depth.
